{
  "_comment": [
    "eiermann-fi2.5 — the ONE place the report table's column titles and the",
    "enum label maps live, because they have TWO consumers and only one of them",
    "is a template:",
    "",
    "  • report.typ and summary.typ merge this into their own STRINGS dict via",
    "    zv_report_common.typ's resolveStrings, so `S.checkState` reads exactly",
    "    as if it had been declared inline;",
    "  • report.pb.js reads the same file to write the CSV, which has no",
    "    template layer to translate in. It is the only place in pb_hooks that",
    "    localizes anything, and it does so from here rather than from a second",
    "    copy of these strings.",
    "",
    "Keeping two copies is how a renamed state ends up spelled one way in the",
    "PDF and another in the CSV OF THE SAME EXPORT — a discrepancy nobody",
    "notices until somebody compares them.",
    "",
    "Only plain strings live here. Anything that is a Typst CLOSURE (a",
    "pluralising count, a period phrase) necessarily stays in the template:",
    "JSON cannot hold a function.",
    "",
    "An unmapped wire value is printed AS ITSELF by both consumers (Typst's",
    "`lbl`, the hook's own lookup). An enum this build does not know is not",
    "something either may guess at — and a report that prints `not_reachable`",
    "is ugly, while one that prints a guess is wrong."
  ],
